{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And Esav saw that Yitzhak blessed Yaakov — in these latter blessings he gave him the land of Canaan that was given to Avraham, and also told him to take a wife from his family, and also commanded him not to take from the daughters of Canaan. Esav thought in his heart: What I married from the daughters of Canaan robbed me of the blessing of Avraham. So he took the daughter of Yishmael, from the family of Avraham; he thought in his heart: perhaps from now on I will merit the inheritance of Avraham."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:29.917597611Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}